# P3-1 Task 6 fixture (-hide cross-module isolation, §1a/§1b R1).
#
# A DIFFERENT module from `hide_owner.clausal` that declares the SAME bare
# spelling (`hide_secret`) but only via `-private` -- an ordinary global
# atom (§1b/R2: global by spelling, no per-module identity), NOT hidden.
# `reaches/1` therefore binds the plain global str `"hide_secret"`, which
# is a different value from `hide_owner`'s mangled `hide_secret` and does
# NOT unify with it -- see
# tests/test_hide_directive.py::test_cross_module_same_spelling_does_not_unify.

-module(hide_other, [reaches/1])
-private([hide_secret])

reaches(hide_secret),
